description:
parser.rs's DeclaratorParser::parse_base_type (around line 1244-1276) only
handles `struct Name` / `union Name` / `enum Name` as a bare tag reference:
if the token after struct/union/enum isn't an Ident, it hard-panics
("expected struct/union/enum tag name") instead of trying to parse an inline
`{ ... }` body. This blocks any member (or parameter, or nested declaration)
whose type is an anonymous or named struct/union/enum defined inline, e.g.:

  struct sigevent {
    union sigval sigev_value;
    int          sigev_signo;
    int          sigev_notify;
    union {
      char  __pad[64 - 2 * sizeof(int) - sizeof(union sigval)];
      pid_t sigev_notify_thread_id;
      struct {
        void  (*sigev_notify_function)(union sigval);
        void *sigev_notify_attributes;
      } __sev_thread;
    } __sev_fields;
  };

found in libc-shim/include/signal.h:33-45 (reached via add.c's #include <stdio.h>).

Two compounding gaps, both need fixing:

1. parse_tag_definition's struct/union field-splitting (parser.rs ~line
   383-393) assumes each field is exactly one PPNode (physical source line)
   and calls self.parse_declaration(text) per node. A nested struct/union
   body spans multiple physical lines/PPNodes, so this needs to accumulate
   nodes (tracking brace depth via lex()'d LBrace/RBrace tokens) until depth
   returns to 0 and the joined text ends in a top-level `;`, then parse the
   joined text as one field declaration -- mirroring how matching_brace()
   already does multi-line detection for function bodies.

2. Once a field's full text (including the nested body) reaches
   DeclaratorParser::parse_base_type, that function still only accepts a
   bare tag name after struct/union/enum. It needs to also accept:
   - no name at all (anonymous tag) followed directly by `{`
   - a name followed by `{` (named nested definition)
   and in both cases parse the brace-delimited field list into fields,
   producing CType::Tagged plus (probably) a new Decl::Record/EnumDecl
   registered somewhere, OR extending CType::Tagged to optionally carry the
   inline body so sema/codegen can see the fields without a separate tag
   registration. This is a design decision -- worth checking how
   RecordDecl/EnumDecl are looked up elsewhere (by name) before picking the
   representation, since anonymous tags have no name to look up by.

